<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12528" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-δοτέον</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one must give</i> to another <i>as</i> his <i>due,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1163a8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				b20
			</span></i>; <i>one must refer, assign,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίτινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					452a
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one must describe, represent,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷος τυγχάνει ὁ θεὸς ὤν . .
			ἀ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				379a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>one must explain, interpret,</i> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				5.25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>one must allow, permit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.73c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δοτέος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
					<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
			<i>to bereferred, ascribed, assigned,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				456b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕτερος ἄν εἴη ὁρισμὸς -τέος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Top.</u>
					142a1
				</span></i>
			. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δοτήρ, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>, ὁ,</span>
			<i>a giver back, repayer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				116
			</span></i>.</div>
